&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is hiring a Health and Safety Specialist to lead the day-to-day H&amp;amp;S work at our San Francisco headquarters and across our broader US footprint. As Anthropic continues to scale, we need someone in the room — operating our health and safety programs, responding to what comes up, and being the trusted face of H&amp;amp;S for our employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who&#39;s spent their career doing the hands-on work of occupational health and safety — running inspections, investigating incidents, managing cases through to closure, supporting committees and emergency response teams, and getting employees engaged in the programs we run. This is a tactical, execution-focused role: you&#39;ll operate the programs we have, contribute to the ones we&#39;re building, and free up the EHS Lead to focus on the broader strategy and the specialty environments (biolabs, data centers, robotics) that need dedicated attention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t be doing this alone. You&#39;ll partner closely with the EHS Lead, with our Workplace, Security, HR, and Legal teams in SF, and with cross-functional partners at our other US offices. As we expand the broader Global Safety and Intelligence Services team, you&#39;ll have peers around you to collaborate with on shared work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll run the regular cadence of onsite H&amp;amp;S work at our San Francisco office — inspections, hazard and risk assessments, ergonomics program activities, and follow-through on the findings. You&#39;ll investigate workplace incidents, injuries, and illnesses, and you&#39;ll manage occupational health cases through their full lifecycle — from initial report through return-to-work and closure — coordinating with our occupational health providers, HR, and Legal partners. You&#39;ll also own OSHA recordkeeping for our US sites, including the annual 300/300A process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be the in-the-room face of H&amp;amp;S for our SF employees and partners. That means facilitating and supporting our health and safety committee and volunteer emergency response team in SF — running meetings, coordinating drills, and following through on action items — and supporting similar work at our other US sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll deliver and coordinate H&amp;amp;S training across our US offices — keeping our training calendar current, running sessions where helpful, and partnering with vendors and internal teams where it makes sense. You&#39;ll manage H&amp;amp;S vendor relationships (occupational health, ergonomics, training, audit) and engage with landlords, building management, and contractors to make sure shared environments are safe and meet our standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll keep our H&amp;amp;S documentation, registers, and reporting systems accurate and current, and you&#39;ll contribute to the broader H&amp;amp;S programs the EHS Lead is building — sharing what you&#39;re seeing in the field, helping pilot new programs at SF, and bringing tactical know-how to standards work as it comes up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 7+ years of experience in a similar hands-on H&amp;amp;S role, ideally with time spent operating H&amp;amp;S programs day-to-day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong working knowledge of US federal OSHA and California Title 8 (Cal/OSHA) requirements; familiarity with other US states (Washington, New York) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable being the H&amp;amp;S expert in the room — translating regulatory requirements into clear decisions, and pushing back when something isn&#39;t safe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about workplace H&amp;amp;S, and bring that energy to the people you work with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have an ability to motivate and persuade others to collaborate, take action, and engage with H&amp;amp;S-related programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are resilient and adaptable in fast-paced, dynamic environments — comfortable with ambiguity and able to prioritize when everything looks urgent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear, useful SOPs, playbooks, and program documents, and can create engaging presentations and training content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience with software tools for H&amp;amp;S incident reporting, risk assessment, learning management, and related functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree in Occupational Health and Safety or another H&amp;amp;S-related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications such as CSP, ASP/GSP, CIH, or COHN — or comparable US-recognized H&amp;amp;S/occupational-health credentials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ISO 45001 (Occupational Health and Safety Management Systems)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in occupational health, fire safety, or industrial hygiene&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating H&amp;amp;S programs across multiple US states or sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent computer skills — quick to pick up new applications and systems at the user and/or administrator level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an onsite role based out of our San Francisco office. We&#39;re looking for someone who wants to be present in the office consistently — typically at least four days per week. The work is in-person by nature: engaging with employees, inspections, drills, committees, incident response, and the kind of in-the-room presence that builds trust with everyone in the workplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll occasionally travel to our other US offices (Seattle, New York City) as needed to support inspections, drills, audits, and incident response. We expect this to land in the 5–10% range, varying by quarter and incident volume.&lt;/p&gt;
