&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s GTM Systems team builds and operates the systems and processes behind the company&#39;s go-to-market motion — quoting, provisioning, customer success tooling, and the data infrastructure that ties them together. As a Program Manager on the team, you&#39;ll own cross-functional coordination across our concurrent systems initiatives: aligning stakeholders, running quarterly business reviews, and making sure every program stays tied to the business outcome it exists to drive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work across Sales, Customer Success, Revenue Operations, Deal Desk, and Business Technology leadership to keep multiple in-flight programs moving in lockstep — CPQ, deployment tracking, account data quality, and compliance-driven process change. You&#39;ll be the person in the room translating between technical implementation detail and executive priorities, and the person following up afterward to make sure alignment turns into action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a typical week, you&#39;ll prepare for and run quarterly business reviews, meet with operational leads and stakeholders across the GTM organization, and pull together the documentation that keeps initiatives aligned. Throughout, you&#39;ll dig into the &quot;why&quot; behind each program — not just tracking status, but making sure the team can always articulate the business outcome a program is meant to drive and how it&#39;s being measured.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own cross-functional coordination across concurrent GTM systems programs, including CPQ, deployment tracking, account data quality, and compliance-driven process change&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare and run quarterly business reviews for GTM systems initiatives, and drive the decisions and follow-ups that come out of them&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with operational leads and stakeholders across Sales, Customer Success, Revenue Operations, Deal Desk, and Business Technology to keep programs aligned and moving&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate between technical implementation detail and executive priorities in both directions, so engineers understand the business context and leadership understands the trade-offs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define and track the business outcome each program exists to drive, along with how it&#39;s measured, and hold programs to it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aggregate and maintain the documentation, plans, and status views that keep cross-functional initiatives coherent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Surface risks, dependencies, and competing priorities early, and drive them to resolution without direct authority over the teams involved&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
