&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team member on the Product Partnerships team at Anthropic, you&#39;ll own the analytical foundation behind how Anthropic thinks about the value of data and product partnerships. You&#39;ll build the valuation frameworks that inform where we invest, and serve as the analytical partner to deal leads through negotiations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your ability to bring analytical rigor to open-ended questions, and to think broadly about the technology and content ecosystem, will serve you well in this role. This is a great fit for someone who thrives in ambiguity, can seamlessly pivot between high-level strategy and detailed analysis, and gets energy from solving problems that don&#39;t have an established playbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Analysis and Valuation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the valuation frameworks used across data and product partnerships, and develop new approaches as partnerships evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the valuation models, partnership evaluation frameworks, and ROI analyses behind partnership initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a benchmark library of comparable transactions and historical pricing, and conduct industry and competitive research to inform strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the internal expert on partnership spend, historical transactions, and forward planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take the team&#39;s most complex challenges from ambiguity to clarity, and prepare the analyses and recommendations to address them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Support and Negotiation Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review inbound proposals and pricing from partners, and provide deal leads with a defensible analytical view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with deal leads to develop negotiation strategies grounded in data, and support partner managers in navigating novel partnership structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable systems and processes that enable the team to grow impact efficiently, leveraging Claude to build them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and reporting infrastructure to track portfolio health, deal pipeline, spend, usage, and key success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize the partnership lifecycle: sourcing, inbound tracking, contracts, cross-functional approvals, delivery, and feedback loops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the liaison between Partnerships, Research, Product and Finance, and work closely with xfn teams to address operational challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You May Be a Good Fit If You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 5+ years of experience in management consulting, investment banking, private equity, growth equity, venture capital, or internal strategy and operations at a technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have exceptional analytical skills and advanced proficiency in financial modeling — you can build and maintain models from the ground up, and you enjoy the craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to influence and align diverse stakeholders (Research, Product, Partnerships, Finance, Legal)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to take full ownership of a workstream and drive it independently from question to decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The judgment and conviction to form an opinion and defend it, paired with the openness to update it as the data evolves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ramp quickly on unfamiliar subject matter — you can identify what drives value in a new domain before you&#39;re an expert in it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build processes and systems from 0 to 1, and leave behind frameworks others can run without you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reach for AI by default — when facing a repetitive analysis, your instinct is to build the tooling rather than grind through it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are excited about Anthropic&#39;s mission to build safe, transformative AI systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
